<title>UK: Mondex grants Central American franchise.</title>
<headline>Mondex grants Central American franchise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payment smartcard organisation Mondex International said on Wednesday it has awarded the franchise rights for seven Central American countries to Credomatic International Corp.</p>
<p>The deal gives Credomatic the exclusive right to develop the Mondex card in Costa Rica, Guatemala, Nicaragua, Panama, Honduras, El Salvador and Belize.</p>
<p>Privately held Credomatic is a major issuer, acquirer and processing agant of credit and debit cards in Central America.</p>
<p>Mondex said the first commercial development in Central America will be a pilot in Costa Rica in the near future.</p>
<p>Mondex is 51 percent owned by international payments company MasterCard.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8864</p>
